Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:18:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] session.resume: a live turn lease on an old chat is
 a typed refusal, not -32603 (self-heal gateway-56086c8e65)

Adopting a not-yet-adopted local chat (session.resume -> adopt_legacy_session ->
bind_legacy_target) ran require_idle, whose transcript guard raises
SessionTurnLeaseLostError / SessionCompressionInProgressError for another writer's
live lease or lock. Nothing translated them, so they escaped the session
dispatcher and the ws boundary answered JSON-RPC -32603 "internal error".

- bind_legacy_target: translate MUTATION_GUARD_REFUSALS at the call: a live turn
  lease -> runtime_coordination_required (the refusal the next check already meant
  to give), a compression lock -> busy_refusal (session_busy, field=compression).
- AuthorityConnection.dispatch: backstop for any caller that still forgets: reply
  4001 busy_refusal(exc) and log one WARNING "untranslated mutation guard refusal
  method=<m>" so the missed caller stays visible.

Why-chain: root (happened) = each writer must translate the guard's refusal type
(MUTATION_GUARD_REFUSALS, f13a1cd2290) and the adoption path (cb748e7a193) predates
it; root (not caught) = migration tests only covered an active-session registry
entry, never a bare DB lease, and no dispatcher test fed a guard refusal.

Proof: tests/gateway/test_legacy_adoption_turn_lease.py (4 tests) red on
aaf655ac4b4, green here; mutants (drop compression translation, flip the lease
branch, demote the WARNING) each fail it; 191 related files / 1484 tests green.
